    <section id="about" style="padding:60px 0 30px 0;max-width:900px;margin:auto;">
        <h2>About</h2>
        <div style="line-height:1.8;font-size:0.95em;">
            <ul>
            <li>Currently, I serve as Algorithm Director at an AI LLM application innovation company, responsible for intelligent agent architecture and reinforcement learning. I am also a member of the Hangzhou Artificial Intelligence Society.</li> 
            <li>Previously, I served as Algorithm Director at Fushu Technology; Algorithm Expert at Wacai and Beibei Group; Visiting Scholar at Tencent; R&D Engineer at Sunyard; and a core contributor to the Yitao R&D promotion system. I have also received algorithm expert offers from top companies such as Didi Chuxing, Youzan, and JD.com.</li>
            <li>My current focus is on large language model (LLM) agents and reinforcement learning. I design agent architectures, tool-use and planning strategies, and evaluation frameworks to improve reliability, autonomy, and task success. Previously, I pioneered privacy-computing algorithms and platforms that won industry awards and were deployed in production. My broader interests include multimodal agents, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and scalable training/evaluation systems for LLM applications.</li>
            <li>Educational background in Computer Science, with primary supervision from Professor Mingsheng Shang at the University of Electronic Science and Technology of China (UESTC), and additional mentorship from Professors Xiaopu Han, Zike Zhang, and Linyuan Lü — now Ph.D. advisors at Zhejiang University and the University of Science and Technology of China.In 2014, participated as a visiting student at Beijing Normal University, under the supervision of Professor Wenxu Wang, focusing on complex networks and network reconstruction.Completed secondary education at Jinhua No.1 High School in Zhejiang Province, Science track, with a top-tier entrance score exceeding the national elite university admission thresholds.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>
